---
// Architecture component - How TIS RMS works on campus
---

<section id="architecture" class="relative bg-[#f8fafc] py-20 border-t border-slate-200">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8">

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full border border-emerald-200 bg-[#ecfdf5] px-3.5 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-[#15803d] uppercase tracking-wider mb-3.5">
        How It's Set Up
      </div>
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">
        Works on your school's network — no internet needed.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        TIS RMS runs on a designated school computer. Teachers connect through the school Wi-Fi or cable network. Everything stays inside the school.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 3 network cards -->
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-3">

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-7 text-center shadow-xs transition hover:shadow-md hover:border-slate-300">
        <div class="flex h-14 w-14 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-slate-100 text-3xl mx-auto mb-4">🖥️</div>
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">Teacher Computers</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Teachers use the Windows desktop app on their workstations or the Android app on their phones to scan documents.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border-2 border-[#15803d]/40 bg-[#ecfdf5] p-7 text-center shadow-xs relative">
        <span class="absolute -top-3 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 rounded-full bg-[#15803d] px-3 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-white shadow-xs">
          Campus Host
        </span>
        <div class="flex h-14 w-14 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-white text-3xl mx-auto mb-4 shadow-xs">🏫</div>
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-[#15803d]">School Server PC</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
          One designated school computer acts as the server. It stores all records and runs quietly in the background — always on.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-7 text-center shadow-xs transition hover:shadow-md hover:border-slate-300">
        <div class="flex h-14 w-14 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-slate-100 text-3xl mx-auto mb-4">📡</div>
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">School Wi-Fi / LAN</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          All devices communicate through the local school network. No data leaves the campus — private and fast.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- 3 benefit cards -->
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-3">

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-6 shadow-xs">
        <h4 class="font-display text-base font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-[#15803d]">✓</span> Works Without Internet
        </h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Teachers can access and update records even when the school's internet connection is slow or down.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-6 shadow-xs">
        <h4 class="font-display text-base font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-[#15803d]">✓</span> Student Data Stays Private
        </h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          All student records are stored only on school hardware — never uploaded to any external service or cloud.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-6 shadow-xs">
        <h4 class="font-display text-base font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-[#15803d]">✓</span> Fast Local Performance
        </h4>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Because everything runs on your local network, searching and loading records is instant across all workstations.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>
